===============================================================================
Third-party components
===============================================================================

The `kvm` and `whp` cargo features add only ordinary Rust dependencies and
talk to the host kernel or hypervisor; they vendor nothing into this repository
(though cargo does link them into the binary like any other dependency):

    kvm-ioctls    Apache-2.0 OR MIT     Linux
    kvm-bindings  Apache-2.0            Linux   <- no MIT option; see above
    libc          MIT OR Apache-2.0     Linux
    windows-sys   MIT OR Apache-2.0     Windows

Vendored in vendor/ (see vendor/README.md for provenance):

* vendor/bochs/ (the `bochs` cargo feature)
    The Bochs CPU sources — libcpu, libfpu, libavx, libcpudb, libsoftfloat and
    four of Bochs' own support sources (logio.cc, gui/siminterface.cc,
    gui/paramtree.cc, pc_system.cc) — compiled by build.rs into this crate's
    native archive and statically linked. Upstream files, except for the bug
    fixes in patches/bochs/, which scripts/vendor-bochs.sh applies on top. Those
    patches are the record of what was changed and why — they are kept as
    separate files, rather than as edits with in-line notes, so the
    modification stays visible and reversible; vendor/bochs/PROVENANCE names
    the ones applied, alongside the exact revision and ./configure flags, and
    scripts/vendor-bochs.sh reproduces the whole tree. `BOCHS_DIR` builds a
    different source root instead.
    License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, which the patches in patches/bochs/ inherit as
    modifications of these files. Copyright (c) the Bochs Project. Full texts in
    vendor/bochs/COPYING and vendor/bochs/LICENSE.
    >> Linking these makes a distributed binary a combined work under the LGPL:
    >> provide the Bochs source — it is vendored here — and allow relinking.
    >> Building with only the default `sail` feature does not involve Bochs
    >> at all.

* vendor/sail/model.cpp.gz, vendor/sail/model.h, vendor/sail/model_missing.cpp
    Generated from rems-project/sail-x86-from-acl2 (the Sail x86 model
    translated from the ACL2 x86isa books).
    License: BSD-3-Clause (Sail model: Copyright (c) 2020 Patrick Taylor;
    2021-2023 Thomas Bauereiss) AND BSD-3-Clause (original ACL2 X86isa model:
    Copyright (c) 2015 Regents of the University of Texas — Shilpi Goel,
    Warren A. Hunt, Jr., Matt Kaufmann et al.; see the sail-x86-from-acl2
    repository's model/LICENSE for both full texts).

* vendor/sail/runtime/{sail,rts,sail_failure,sail_config}.{c,h} (patched)
    The Sail C runtime, from the `sail` package.
    License: BSD-2-Clause. Copyright (c) the Sail authors / contributors
    (University of Cambridge et al.).

* vendor/sail/runtime/cJSON.{c,h}
    License: MIT. Copyright (c) 2009-2017 Dave Gamble and cJSON contributors.

* vendor/sail/runtime/mini-gmp.{c,h}, mini-mpq.{c,h}
    From GMP 6.3.0. License: dual LGPL-3.0-or-later OR GPL-2.0-or-later.
    Copyright (c) the Free Software Foundation, Inc.
    >> This is the only copyleft component in a DEFAULT build (a
    >> `--features bochs` build also links Bochs, LGPL-2.1-or-later — see
    >> above). It is bundled and statically linked by default, so
    >> redistributing a built binary triggers the LGPL's obligations
    >> (provide the GMP source — included here — and allow relinking).
    >> Building with SAIL_SYSTEM_GMP links the system libgmp instead, which
    >> is LGPL all the same. Full GMP license texts:
    >> https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.html and
    >> https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.html
